In the meantime adding this to your babel plugins solves it:

```
["@babel/plugin-transform-react-jsx", {
  "pragmaFrag": "React.Fragment"
}]
```

review_comments:
@devongovett There is no official support for fragments in [Preact](https://github.com/developit/preact/issues/946), [NervJS](https://github.com/NervJS/nerv/issues/5), and [HyperApp](https://github.com/jorgebucaran/hyperapp/issues/530).

Can't we merge this PR for now and add support for those libraries when they officially support it? It's frustrating to have to add a config for something that is supported to be the [default option](https://babeljs.io/docs/en/babel-plugin-transform-react-jsx#pragmafrag) in Babel.

We are literally forcing users to do more configuration than the default Babel behaviour.
